MathCAT: keep an empty argument an intent refers to (e.g. an empty naryand)

UnicodeMathML builds `∫▒` with an empty integrand as
`<mrow intent=":nary(,,$naryand)"><mo>∫</mo><mrow arg="naryand"><mspace/></mrow></mrow>`.
Canonicalization turns the mspace into a whitespace `mtext` (nbsp), lifts
it into the `arg="naryand"` mrow, and `merge_whitespace` then removes it as
mere spacing: the intent's `$naryand` refers to nothing, and the empty
integrand is not a node anyone can navigate to. Mathessible keeps half-typed
equations built (a zero-width space stands in for the missing integrand,
see src/mathessible/build_repair.py) and needs that empty argument as a node, so
a whitespace mtext carrying `arg` is no longer treated as spacing.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of upstream 85c89a37. Worth
proposing upstream to daisy/MathCAT (an intent referring to a removed
child is a bug on its own).

diff --git a/src/canonicalize.rs b/src/canonicalize.rs
index 0ccf108f..dc01963a 100644
--- a/src/canonicalize.rs
+++ b/src/canonicalize.rs
@@ -2025,7 +2025,9 @@ impl CanonicalizeContext {
 			let mut whitespace: Option<f64> = None;
 			while i < children.len() {
 				let child = as_element(children[i]);
-				let is_child_whitespace = name(child) == "mtext" && as_text(child) == "\u{00A0}";
+				// An argument an intent refers to (e.g. the empty naryand of `:nary(,,$naryand)`) is not
+				// spacing: removing it leaves the intent pointing at nothing.
+				let is_child_whitespace = name(child) == "mtext" && as_text(child) == "\u{00A0}" && child.attribute("arg").is_none();
